The implementation source is the exact revision above; its CMake file has one
packaging-only change that uses the checked-in libjpeg-turbo source instead of a
network download. It is built with UHDR_WRITE_XMP=ON and
UHDR_WRITE_ISO=OFF by nc's dependency feature selection. Do not replace it with
an unreviewed release tarball: nc relies on the merged metadata-writing fix.

The `third_party/turbojpeg` directory is libjpeg-turbo 3.1.0 at revision
20ade4dea9589515a69793e447a6c6220b464535, the version selected by this
libultrahdr CMake snapshot. CMake's network download is disabled; the archive is
built and linked statically.

`scripts/check-vendored-native.py` mechanically verifies separate deterministic
tree hashes for the libultrahdr snapshot and bundled libjpeg-turbo snapshot.
The copied upstream tree retains its own `.gitignore`; broad upstream patterns
such as `build*` and `tests/data` would otherwise cause ordinary `git add` to
omit real snapshot files while they remain present locally. Those files are
intentionally force-added, and the verifier checks that every hashed file is in
the Git index so a clean CI checkout hashes the same tree. This local-vendoring
workaround and its verifier are removed by
`output/ultrahdr-dependency-externalization` (see
`docs/tasks/output/ultrahdr-dependency-externalization.md`).
The only modification inside the pinned libultrahdr tree is packaging-only:
`CMakeLists.txt` points ExternalProject at the checked-in turbojpeg tree and
sets `DOWNLOAD_COMMAND ""`. No codec or image-science source is modified.
